{"name":"Garden Gate","hex":"#dadcc1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden gate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gate leading to a garden.","The number eight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden_gate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden Gate, Bulandshahr","blocks":[{"text":"Garden Gate is a building in Bulandshahr, India, constructed as a gateway to the Bulandshahr public garden, also known as Moti Bagh. It leads to the Town Hall and was built in the late 19th century by Rao Umrao Singh of Kuchesar, who donated a significant fund for its construction. The project was encouraged by Frederic Growse, a British civil servant of the Indian Civil Service, who had been appointed collector of the region in 1878."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_%281880s%29.png/330px-Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_%281880s%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr","wikidata":"Q112169040"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"},{"title":"Gate","blocks":[{"text":"A gate or gateway is a point of entry to or from a space enclosed by walls or other barriers. The word is derived from Proto-Germanic *gatan, meaning an opening or passageway. Synonyms include portal. The concept originally referred to the gap or hole in the wall or fence, rather than a barrier which closed it. Gates may prevent or control the entry or exit of individuals, or they may be merely decorative. The moving part or parts of a gateway may be considered \"doors\", as they are fixed at one side whilst opening and closing like one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg/330px-Gate_of_the_BCR_Headquarters_Building_%28Bucharest%2C_Romania%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gate","wikidata":"Q53060"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif/lossless-page1-120px-Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif/lossless-page1-250px-Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif/lossless-page1-120px-Bulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABulandhar_Garden_Gate_night_view.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_2023%2C_rear.tif/lossless-page1-120px-Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_2023%2C_rear.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_2023%2C_rear.tif/lossless-page1-250px-Garden_Gate%2C_Bulandshahr_2023%2C_rear.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo